  "summary": "Malicious code in @shared-web/assets (npm)",
  "details": "The install hook of this package (advertised as an asset-resolution library) runs `node index.js`, which loads lib/core.js. That module collects the local username, hostname, and current working directory, encodes them together with a Unix timestamp into a single DNS query string, and resolves it against the domain oob[.]algamil7x[.]xyz — a DNS beacon that exfiltrates host metadata to a remote server. The strings are hidden behind charcode-array decoding to evade inspection.",
